{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n \\\"prize|ERC-721|untrusted|releaseSponsorPrize|sponsorRecipient|transferFrom\\\" DESIGN.md; sed -n '1,260p' DESIGN.md\"","aggregated_output":"2:Ethereum NFT raffle; immutable factory, ERC-1167 clones with immutable implementation. One entry costs 1,000,000 units of canonical six-decimal USDC. One purchase mints a transferable ERC721 ticket representing a contiguous inclusive range. Exactly one ERC721 prize is escrowed atomically at creation. Reserve met awards NFT and 95% sponsor / 5% treasury. Reserve missed awards 80% gross to winner, 15% sponsor, 5% treasury. Refund outcome pays 100% per entry and returns prize. Rounding is floor on aggregate protocol fee; remainder must be allocated without loss. No administrator, mutable configuration or upgrade. Request window [sale end, end+2days); callback accepted strictly before request timestamp+2days. Refunds open at deadline. Callback records result only. Settlement is permissionless, storage-only; redemption requires current ticket owner, burns claim atomically, and must revert all effects on delivery failure. Sponsor and treasury can claim independently after settlement. Never move assets between raffle clones. Quote token and Chainlink wrapper are trusted canonical dependencies; arbitrary prize contracts and ticket recipients are untrusted. Frontend discovery is advisory; transaction decisions must reread current chain state.\n# Clean design specification\nEthereum NFT raffle; immutable factory, ERC-1167 clones with immutable implementation. One entry costs 1,000,000 units of canonical six-decimal USDC. One purchase mints a transferable ERC721 ticket representing a contiguous inclusive range. Exactly one ERC721 prize is escrowed atomically at creation. Reserve met awards NFT and 95% sponsor / 5% treasury. Reserve missed awards 80% gross to winner, 15% sponsor, 5% treasury. Refund outcome pays 100% per entry and returns prize. Rounding is floor on aggregate protocol fee; remainder must be allocated without loss. No administrator, mutable configuration or upgrade. Request window [sale end, end+2days); callback accepted strictly before request timestamp+2days. Refunds open at deadline. Callback records result only. Settlement is permissionless, storage-only; redemption requires current ticket owner, burns claim atomically, and must revert all effects on delivery failure. Sponsor and treasury can claim independently after settlement. Never move assets between raffle clones. Quote token and Chainlink wrapper are trusted canonical dependencies; arbitrary prize contracts and ticket recipients are untrusted. Frontend discovery is advisory; transaction decisions must reread current chain state.\n\nThis specification was composed before scanner results and historical findings. Source, not design prose, determines actual behavior. No tests, audit history, accepted-risk lists or scanner results are provided.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":false,\"stub_explanation\":\"\",\"results\":[{\"flow_summary\":\"During an otherwise eligible release, the configured prize token can synchronously reenter releaseSponsorPrize. The shared reentrancy guard rejects the nested invocation before its body executes; if the token propagates that error, the outer release also reverts. If the token catches it, execution rejoins the ownership-verification routes below.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:395 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - the outer permissionless invocation enters the nonReentrant modifier.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - verifies the guard is clear and marks it ENTERED.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:403 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - marks prizeClaimed before handing control to the prize token.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:404 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - dynamically invokes the untrusted configured prize token, which may attempt a synchronous callback.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:395 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - the prize token dispatches a nested invocation of the same entrypoint.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:88 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBeforeView - observes ENTERED and reverts at line 90 with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"If uncaught by the prize token, ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall propagates through transferFrom and reverts the complete outer transaction, restoring prizeClaimed and all token-side state.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol\",\"flow_line\":90,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The release caller supplies no arguments and controls only call timing. Transfer parameters are fixed as from=address(this), to=stored sponsorRecipient, and tokenId=stored prizeTokenId; the nested invocation comes from configured token behavior rather than forwarded caller data.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"The NFT transfer is the function's untrusted-code boundary. The guard prevents that external code from recursively entering protected raffle operations while prizeClaimed and token ownership may be in transition.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"A call made before a terminal outcome—while status is AwaitingPrize, Active, or Drawing—is rejected before the claimed flag is changed or any NFT call occurs.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:395 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - dispatches the no-argument permissionless entrypoint through nonReentrant.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - acquires the shared guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:396 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - reads the current lifecycle status.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:397 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - determines that the status is neither CashWon nor Refunding.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:398 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - reverts with SponsorPrizeUnavailable(currentStatus).\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"SponsorPrizeUnavailable is returned as a transaction-reverting custom error; no persistent state change or external asset call occurs.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":397,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"There are no calldata arguments and no asset sink is reached. The caller-controlled timing determines whether the stored status is still AwaitingPrize, Active, or Drawing; caller identity is not an authorization input.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This lifecycle boundary prevents permissionless callers from removing the escrowed NFT before prize deposit, during entry sales, or while randomness is pending.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"When the reserve was met and status is NftWon, releaseSponsorPrize rejects the sponsor-return route before checking prizeClaimed, preserving the NFT redemption path for the winning ticket owner.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:395 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - dispatches the permissionless entrypoint through nonReentrant.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - acquires the shared guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:396 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - reads NftWon from storage.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:397 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - NftWon fails both accepted-status comparisons.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:398 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - reverts with SponsorPrizeUnavailable(Status.NftWon).\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"SponsorPrizeUnavailable(NftWon) reverts the transaction without changing state or calling the prize token.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":397,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"No asset sink is reached. The caller supplies no arguments; timing after an NFT-winning resolution is the only relevant caller-controlled circumstance, and msg.sender is not authorized specially.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This outcome is economically distinct from premature calls: it prevents the sponsor-release mechanism from competing with the winning ticket owner's claim to the escrowed NFT.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"In CashWon or Refunding status, a second or later release attempt is rejected when prizeClaimed is already true. Status is checked first and remains unchanged after a successful prior release.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:395 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - enters the permissionless function through nonReentrant.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - acquires the shared guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:397 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - accepts the stored CashWon or Refunding status.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:400 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - observes prizeClaimed and reverts with PrizeAlreadyClaimed.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"PrizeAlreadyClaimed reverts the transaction before recipient loading or an external NFT call.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":400,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"No asset sink is reached. The caller supplies no arguments; transaction ordering and timing after a prior successful release determine that prizeClaimed is true.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"The one-time claim boundary prevents repeated permissionless attempts to transfer the same escrowed prize and makes racing callers resolve atomically.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"With an eligible status and unclaimed prize, the function marks the prize claimed and calls the configured prize token's transferFrom. If that dynamic call fails or reverts, the error propagates and all effects roll back.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:395 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - enters through nonReentrant.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:397 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - accepts CashWon or Refunding.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:400 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - confirms the prize is unclaimed.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:402 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - loads the write-once sponsorRecipient from storage.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:403 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - sets prizeClaimed=true before the interaction.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:404 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - dynamically calls prizeToken.transferFrom(address(this), recipient, prizeTokenId).\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol:91 IERC721.transferFrom - dispatches to the arbitrary configured ERC-721 implementation without requiring a recipient acceptance callback.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"The prize token's call failure or revert bubbles to the caller; the EVM rolls back prizeClaimed, token state changes, and logs.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":404,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The external caller controls only when release is invoked. The NFT sink receives fixed stored values: from=the raffle, to=sponsorRecipient, and tokenId=prizeTokenId; the NFT contract sees the raffle, not the release caller, as msg.sender.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the custody-moving external-call boundary to an explicitly untrusted prize contract. Checks-effects-interactions and transaction atomicity protect the claim state, but successful delivery and liveness depend on the token's transfer implementation.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"The NFT transfer can return successfully but the subsequent ownerOf query can revert or return malformed ABI data. That failure reverts the complete transaction, including the earlier token transfer.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:397 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - accepts CashWon or Refunding.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:400 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - confirms the prize is unclaimed.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:403 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - tentatively marks the prize claimed.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:404 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - transferFrom returns successfully.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:405 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - performs an external ownerOf(prizeTokenId) query whose revert or malformed response prevents ABI decoding.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol:39 IERC721.ownerOf - dynamically dispatches the ownership query to the configured prize token.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"A prize-token revert or Solidity ABI-decoding failure from ownerOf reverts the top-level call and rolls back both prizeClaimed and the preceding NFT transfer.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":405,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller supplies no ownership-query data. Timing selects an eligible state, while ownerOf receives only the stored prizeTokenId and is invoked against the stored prize-token address.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Finalization has a second external dependency after the asset transfer. Atomic rollback prevents partial on-chain completion, while the arbitrary token's query behavior controls whether release can finish.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"If transferFrom returns and ownerOf returns a decodable address other than sponsorRecipient, the explicit delivery postcondition fails and the whole transaction is reverted.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:397 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - accepts CashWon or Refunding.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:400 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - confirms the prize is unclaimed.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:403 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - tentatively sets prizeClaimed=true.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:404 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - the configured token's transferFrom returns successfully.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:405 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - compares ownerOf(prizeTokenId) with sponsorRecipient and reverts on a mismatch.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"PrizeDeliveryVerificationFailed(sponsorRecipient) reverts the transaction, restoring the raffle and token state to their pre-call values.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":405,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The releaser cannot choose the expected owner or token ID. Both sponsorRecipient and prizeTokenId come from stored initialization data; current-call timing is the only controlled input.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This postcondition detects tokens that return from transferFrom without reporting the intended recipient as owner. Its security still depends on the untrusted token truthfully implementing ownerOf.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"After authenticated resolution has produced CashWon because the reserve was missed, any caller can return the escrowed NFT to the fixed sponsorRecipient. Successful reported delivery marks the prize claimed, emits SponsorPrizeReleased, and leaves status as CashWon.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:395 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - dispatches the no-argument permissionless function through nonReentrant.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - acquires the shared guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:396 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - reads CashWon.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:397 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - passes the accepted-status gate.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:400 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - confirms prizeClaimed is false.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:402 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - loads the fixed sponsorRecipient.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:403 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - permanently marks the prize claimed if the transaction completes.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:404 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - calls the configured NFT's transferFrom with the raffle as source and sponsorRecipient as destination.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:405 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - confirms ownerOf(prizeTokenId) reports sponsorRecipient.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:406 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - emits SponsorPrizeReleased with the triggering msg.sender.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:102 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantAfter - clears the guard before the empty successful return.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"The function emits SponsorPrizeReleased, clears the reentrancy guard, and returns successfully with prizeClaimed=true and status still CashWon.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":404,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller controls timing and contributes msg.sender only to event metadata. The asset transfer uses stored prizeToken, prizeTokenId, and sponsorRecipient; it cannot be redirected by the releaser.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This permissionless custody release can occur independently of winning-ticket settlement or cash redemption. The fixed destination limits caller authority, while the arbitrary NFT implementation and unsafe transferFrom boundary warrant review; transferFrom does not mandate an IERC721Receiver callback for a contract recipient.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"After the raffle enters Refunding, any caller can return the escrowed NFT to the fixed sponsorRecipient. Successful reported delivery marks the prize claimed and emits SponsorPrizeReleased without waiting for ticket refunds to complete.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:395 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - dispatches the no-argument permissionless function through nonReentrant.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - acquires the shared guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:396 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - reads Refunding.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:397 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - passes the accepted-status gate.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:400 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - confirms prizeClaimed is false.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:402 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - loads the fixed sponsorRecipient.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:403 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - permanently marks the prize claimed if the transaction completes.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:404 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - calls the configured NFT's transferFrom with the raffle as source and sponsorRecipient as destination.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:405 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - confirms ownerOf(prizeTokenId) reports sponsorRecipient.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:406 Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize - emits SponsorPrizeReleased with the triggering msg.sender.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:102 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantAfter - clears the guard before the empty successful return.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"The function emits SponsorPrizeReleased, clears the reentrancy guard, and returns successfully with prizeClaimed=true and status still Refunding.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":404,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller controls timing and contributes msg.sender only to event metadata. The asset sink receives only stored configuration: prizeToken, prizeTokenId, and sponsorRecipient.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Prize return is intentionally independent of remainingRefundLiability and may occur before, during, or after participant refunds. The releaser cannot redirect the NFT, but delivery crosses the same arbitrary-token boundary and uses transferFrom without a mandated recipient callback.\"}]}"}}
